{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01XxKJ5LV5vaPuow41PkuTKh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Anchor is a single-folder, stdlib-only personal productivity and R&D control system for J.C. Liechty, runtime-rooted at `C:\\dev\\Anchor` and served as a persistent local web app. Grounded claims:\n\n- **Purpose â€” a personal task/project cockpit.** It manages tasks across life domains (academic, commercial, family, writing) as plain markdown files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, `domains/*.md`), with a full task lifecycle: Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled / Saved-for-Later â†’ Restored. Markdown is the single source of truth â€” no database, no binary formats.\n\n- **What it ships â€” `anchor_gui.py`, the declared deliverable.** A self-contained Python stdlib HTTP server that regenerates the full interactive dashboard HTML per request, reads/writes the markdown directly, and runs persistently on `http://localhost:8777` under the NSSM Windows service `anchor` (lifecycle owned by the service, not launched by hand). A CLI mirror (`anchor.py`) shares the same logic and also emits a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **An R&D \"Mission Control\" surface for trio-driven development.** Beyond tasks, it turns each project into a window for the **researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman** trio. v2 added a truthful memory layer: per-lane **sessions**, cached/validated **summaries**, a **Grass Catchers** idea lane, and deliverable declare/pin. v3 \"Mission Control\" added real **ConPTY terminals** (xterm.js over hand-rolled WebSocket/SSE), **per-session git-worktree isolation**, a stacking window manager, in-place expandable summaries, stage **handoffs**, and a guarded runnable **deliverable preview** (ephemeral port, never 8777).\n\n- **Stdlib-only with one declared exception.** Python 3.8+ standard library only, except the v3 terminal subsystem's optional `pywinpty` (`import winpty`, lazy, in `pty_manager.py` only, `pip install .[terminal]`) â€” it degrades gracefully if absent, and `distro.py`'s import scan enforces the rule against any other native/third-party import.\n\n- **Self-verifying.** A daily 5 AM health check (`anchor_healthcheck.py`) parses every markdown file, boots a throwaway server, exercises every endpoint, and walks the full v2 and v3 R&D surfaces fully stubbed (never live `claude`, never the live `:8777` service), writing a dated report and flagging failures with a dashboard banner.\n\n- **Branding.** The home page is presented as a **Ghost World Labs** tool \"powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢,\" using a vendored brand mark served traversal-safe and set as the favicon.\n\nNote: the current branch `foreman/rnd-surface-v4` and the v4 design memory indicate a **v4 redesign** (calm single-screen cockpit, one ConPTY substrate, skill-loads-once) is in flight but not yet built â€” the shipped state is v3, merged to master (commit `208bce1`)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4420,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20430,"cache_read_input_tokens":20573,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20430},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"66678ef8-f9e9-4576-8f7c-4462f2a51382","uuid":"1a8217d8-7048-4020-9100-549404d30219","request_id":"req_011Cbyk7NVT7a413GiWupbYr"}
